# The Key to the Vault: Bot1's equipped Savannah Lions (2/1) deals 2 combat damage to Bot2, so Bot1 looks at exactly the top two
# cards of their library (the third, a Mox Jet, is not among them, so an Arrange naming just two cards is complete only for exactly two), exiles the Shivan Dragon (mana value 6) among them, puts the Island on the bottom and
# casts the Dragon for nothing (CR 608.2g, 118.9). Bot2's own top card, a Shivan Dragon too, stays in Bot2's library.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Sapphire
Mox Jet
Mox Pearl
Mox Ruby
Mox Emerald
The Key to the Vault
Savannah Lions
Plains
Shivan Dragon
Island
Mox Jet
Plains x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Plains x8
Shivan Dragon
Plains x11

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Hand.The Key to the Vault.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Savannah Lions.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.The Key to the Vault.Activate(Bot1.Battlefield.Savannah Lions)
? Bot1.Mana =
Bot1.Attack(Savannah Lions > Bot2)
! Bot1.Arrange(shuffle)
Bot1.Arrange(Shivan Dragon | Island)
Bot1.Accept
[T5 Bot1.Main1]

[Expect]
Bot2.Life = 18
Bot1.Battlefield.Shivan Dragon.Tapped = false
Bot1.Battlefield.Count = 8
Exile.Count = 0
Bot1.Hand = Mox Jet; Plains
Bot1.Library.Count = 11
